r production systems, connect the merged commit to the build artifact and deployment record. This allows engineers to identify exactly which source revision is running, investigate incidents, and reproduce a release when required.\n\n## 10. Interview and Practical Understanding\n\nAn engineer should be able to explain what **Merge Conflict Resolution — Configuration and Access Control — Merge Conflict Resolution [stage-2-topic-9-section-15]** means, why the team needs it, how Git or GitHub implements it, which commands or interface actions are involved, what can go wrong, and how the result is verified.\n\nA strong practical answer describes the repository state before the operation, the exact steps performed, the evidence collected, and the final state. Avoid saying only that a command was executed. Explain what the command changed and how that change was confirmed."
